\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Responding to Requests\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Would you ... ?<br/> I'd like to ...<br/> Would you mind (if) ... ?<br/> Would ... be okay?<br/>Would you mind if ... ? <br/>I was wondering if ...<br/> Could you ... ?<br/> Do you think you could ... ?<br/> Is there any chance you could ... ?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sure, I'll ...<br/> Sure, I'd be glad to ...<br/> No, not at all.<br/> Certainly.<br/> Yes, of course.<br/> I'll see what I can do.<br/> I don't mind at all.<br/> Of course we can ...<br/> No problem.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "&nbsp;", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Simple Past Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Simple Past tense to talk about events or actions that are finished.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "To make questions and negatives in the Simple Past tense, you use the auxiliary <span class=\"italic\">do</span> in the past - <span class=\"italic\">did</span>. The main verb is in the base form - the infinitive without <span class=\"italic\">to </span>(e.g.,ask,understand). ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Negative: <span class=\"italic\"> I didn't understand you.</span><br>Question: <span class=\"italic\">Did you ask me a question?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Simple Past form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"sail<br> bend<br> take<br> keep<br> get\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"sailed<br> bent<br> took<br> kept<br> got\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "We bent down to go inside.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We squeezed against people to get by them! ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "Giza ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the third largest city in Egypt ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I want to visit the Pyramids in Giza.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le11ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you need to review.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "fare", "type": "name"}, {"content": "money paid to travel on a bus, cab or other vehicle ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I gave the bus driver my fare to get on the bus.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le11ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to bend down ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to lower the top part of the body ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I had to bend down to pick up the toy on the floor.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le11ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to squeeze", "type": "name"}, {"content": "manage to get into or through a narrow or restricted space", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We had to squeeze by the people to get through.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le11ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "sail", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to travel on the water in a boat or ship ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The wind made it easy to sail on the large lake.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le11ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "chaotic", "type": "name"}, {"content": "when everything is confusing and out of order ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The streets were so full of traffic and people, things were chaotic.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le11ob11aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write about your vacation in Egypt.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a postcard to your friend.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Say what you did and what you saw.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Give your opinion.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write 50-75 words.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your postcard to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write about my vacation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": " I give my opinion. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read my postcard aloud.", "type": "text"}]}]}